 "producer_cognition_model_dependency_count": 0,
 "read_this_first": "A PILOT, NOT A RUN OF THE BENCHMARK: 23 of the 130 MiniWoB++ pages, chosen by the producer because the change touches them (pages that cannot be done by pressing and typing alone, the three pages hit by the press-point fault, and click-color). The other 107 pages were NOT re-run with this code, so no total over 130 exists for it. Same browser, same search budget (600 actions), same success rule (the page's full reward), one try per instance, 20 instances per page, seeds 1040-1059. What changed since run 4 (V4): (1) a press lands on a part of the element that shows, not on the middle of its box whatever covers it; (2) the hand can also move the pointer onto an element, press three times fast, take hold of an element and let go of it over another, carry one a short way up/down/left/right, and let the seconds the instruction speaks of go by; the guided search tries those only after everything pressing and typing reach; (3) the instruction is read the way the benchmark's own environment reads it for an agent (core.getUtterance), which on one page turns a colour sample into the colour's name; (4) an element reports the colour the page states on it, and text shown as selected is part of what is seen. The learner itself gained only: steps of the new kinds, a word a step carries (direction, seconds) read from the instruction like typed text, and colour as a property an instruction can name. RESULT ON THESE 23 PAGES: a first success was found on 15 (run 4: 6); from one success 8 pages are at 18 of 20 or more (run 4, on its own unseen instances: 0), with three practice instances 10 (run 4: 0). The comparison is across different unseen instances of the same pages (1020-1039 then, 1040-1059 now); the skills run 4 kept were lost with the sandbox and could not be scored on the new ones. 8 of the 23 pages still have no first success, and 5 have one but stay below 18 of 20 even with practice. No task is held out. Before the full run the producer looked at these instances twice: at the wording of a handful of instructions while building the actions, and at the per-instance outcomes of a first pilot on the same seeds. After that first pilot two things were changed, neither in the learner: see instrument_corrections.",
